            <ArticleTitle>Making the most of cholesterol-lowering margarines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>194-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Used as a substitute for normal dietary intake of saturated fatty acids, margarines containing plant sterols can cause a modest reduction in serum total cholesterol and low-density lipoprotein cholesterol levels. They have been shown effective in patients with mild hypercholesterolemia, but they are also useful in the general population.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
